    "https://cottey.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Assistant-Professor-of-Psychology-2026-Updated.pdf": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Psychology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Psychology  \n \nCottey College, a private liberal arts and sciences college for women, invites applications for a full-\ntime, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Psychology position, beginning August 2027. We are \nseeking candidates with experience teaching student-centered courses in Developmental \nPsychology, with preference given to candidates who can also teach a course in Psychology of \nWomen or Sports Psychology. A Ph.D. In Psychology is preferred, along with a strong record of \nundergraduate teaching; however, ABD candidates will be considered and are encouraged to apply. \n \nThis position includes opportunities to become involved with undergraduate research in our \ndedicated Psychology Lab space, which includes computers and an observation room. We are \nseeking candidates who will collaborate with our effective, dynamic department that, in its short \ntime, has successfully sent graduates to careers in behavioral health and counseling, as well as \nseveral graduate programs and research laboratories. In addition to teaching responsibilities, \nfaculty advise and mentor undergraduates, sponsor student organizations, and participate in a \ntight-knit campus community.  \n \nCottey College, located in Nevada, Missouri, has offered young women the opportunity to learn and \ngrow since 1884. It encompasses a diverse group of students, faculty, and staff, including first \ngeneration students, students awarded Pell Grants, students of color, international students, \nfaculty of color, and international faculty. The successful candidate will have demonstrated \nfavorable results in working with diverse populations. A Cottey education is guided by three \nthreads: leadership, social responsibility, and global awareness. Cottey College helps each student \nexcel as learners, leaders, and global citizens - providing a comprehensive and empowering \nexperience in an intimate academic setting that transforms them to reach their highest potential.   \n \nReview of applications begins upon receipt and continues until the position is filled. Send cover \nletter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy that also addresses teaching a diverse \nstudent body, copies of unofficial transcripts, and contact information for three references. \nApplication materials should be submitted by email as PDF documents to Dr. Karla McCain, VPAA, \nCottey College, Nevada, MO 64772. E-mail: acadaffairs@cottey.edu; Phone: 417-667-8181, ext. \n2128. Applicants must be eligible to work in the U.S. without sponsorship. Further information \nabout Cottey is available at http://www.cottey.edu. Cottey College is an Equal Opportunity \nEmployer.  \n \n"
    },
    "https://cottey.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Assistant-Professor-in-Business.pdf": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Business Administration",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Business Administration  \nCottey College, a private liberal arts and sciences college for women, invites \napplications for a full-time, tenure-track position Business Administration, with the \npossibility of starting in January or August 2027. Ideal candidates would have the ability to \nteach a range of courses in business, most especially Operation Management and \nEntrepreneurship courses. The successful candidate will have a record of effective \nteaching and have a doctoral degree or M.B.A. ideally in hand by the start of the contract. \nHighly qualified ABDs will also be considered. We especially encourage applications from \ncandidates with significant professional experience in operations management, \nentrepreneurship, or related fields who are interested in transitioning from industry \npractice into teaching. Practitioner expertise brings real-world relevance to the classroom, \nand we welcome candidates who may not have a traditional academic path but bring deep \nfunctional knowledge, industry connections, and a passion for mentoring the next \ngeneration of business leaders.  \n Typical teaching loads for faculty are three courses per semester. Cottey faculty also \nengage in activities related to scholarly vitality, advise and mentor students, sponsor \nstudent organizations, engage in service, and participate in the life of the college. This \nposition also includes opportunities to contribute to the development of the Clark Institute \nfor Women in Business. Faculty in the Business department are expected to collaborate \nwith their colleagues as well as with students inside and outside the classroom, molding \nexperiential learning and mentoring opportunities.   \n Cottey College, located in Nevada, Missouri, has offered women the opportunity to learn \nand grow since 1884. It encompasses a diverse group of students, faculty, and staff—\nincluding first generation students, Pell Grant students, students of color, and international \nstudents as well as faculty of color and international faculty. A Cottey education is guided \nby three threads: leadership, social responsibility, and global awareness. Cottey College \nhelps each student excel as learners, leaders, and global citizens - providing a \ncomprehensive and empowering experience in an intimate academic setting.       \n  Review of applications begins upon receipt and continues until the position is filled. Send \ncover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy that also addresses \nteaching a diverse student body, copies of unofficial transcripts, and contact information \nfor three references. Application materials should be submitted by email as PDF \ndocuments to Dr. Karla McCain, VPAA, Cottey College, Nevada, MO 64772. E-mail: \nacadaffairs@cottey.edu; Phone: 417-667-8181, ext. 2128. Applicants must be eligible to \nwork in the U.S. without sponsorship. Further information about Cottey is available at \nhttp://www.cottey.edu. Cottey College is an Equal Opportunity Employer.  "
    },
    "https://cottey.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/biology-ad-fall-2026.pdf": {
      "title": "letter; curriculum vitae; statement of teaching philosophy; copies of transcripts, and the contact",
      "description": "Cottey College, a private liberal arts and sciences college for women, invites applications for a full-\ntime, tenure-track position in biology, starting August 2027. We seek candidates to teach an \nintroductory course in cellular and molecular biology and Anatomy & Physiology.  This position \nsupports students majoring in Biology, Biochemistry & Molecular Biology, or Exercise & Sports \nScience. Cottey is a teaching focused institution with a well-equipped teaching laboratory and \nfacilities. Competitive internal funding opportunities are available for faculty professional \ndevelopment, summer research grants, and students doing work with leadership elements. \nResearch is not required, but encouraged. The successful candidate will have a record of effective \nteaching and have doctoral degree in biology, or a closely related discipline, in hand by the start of \nthe contract.  \n   \nCottey College, located in Nevada, Missouri, has offered young women the opportunity to learn and \ngrow since 1884. It encompasses a diverse group of students, faculty, and staff, including first \ngeneration students, students awarded Pell Grants, students of color, international students, \nfaculty of color, and international faculty. The successful candidate will have demonstrated \nfavorable results in working with diverse populations. A Cottey education is guided by three \nthreads: leadership, social responsibility, and global awareness. Cottey College helps each student \nexcel as learners, leaders, and global citizens - providing a comprehensive and empowering \nexperience in an intimate academic setting that transforms them to reach their highest potential.   \n \nReview of application begins upon receipt and continues until the position is filled.  Send cover \nletter; curriculum vitae; statement of teaching philosophy; copies of transcripts, and the contact \ninformation for three references. Application materials should be submitted by email as PDF \ndocuments to Dr. Karla McCain, VPAA, Cottey College, Nevada, MO 64772. E-mail: \nacadaffairs@cottey.edu; Phone: 417-667-8181, ext. 2128. Further information about Cottey is \navailable at http://www.cottey.edu. Cottey College is an Equal Opportunity Employer.  \n "
    },
